# Read committed is what the idempotency replay needs, and inheriting it means a
# change to the connection string can take it away without a line of Go changing.

title: a write inherits its isolation level instead of naming it
file: internal/ledgerhttp/ledgerhttp.go
run: go test -count=1 -run TestPoolLendsAWriteAtReadCommitted -v ./internal/ledgerhttp/
--- before
	tx, err := c.BeginTx(ctx, &sql.TxOptions{Isolation: sql.LevelReadCommitted})
--- after
	tx, err := c.BeginTx(ctx, &sql.TxOptions{Isolation: sql.LevelRepeatableRead})
